llowed by Brave, Hero, and Valor.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"details\",\"2\",{\"className\":\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\",\"children\":\"What cultures have the strongest tradition of courage-based animal names?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Norse and Germanic cultures have a particularly rich tradition of courage-based naming — names like Thor, Odin, Valkyrie, and Bjorn (bear) reflect warrior values. Japanese culture offers samurai-inspired names like Takeshi (warrior) and Isamu (brave). Celtic traditions provide names like Conall (strong wolf) and Brianna (noble, strong). Across cultures, courage-related names signal respect and admiration for the animal bearing them.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"details\",\"3\",{\"className\":\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Can a courageous name actually influence how people perceive my pet?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Yes — name stereotyping is a well-documented psychological phenomenon. A dog named 'Valor' is perceived as braver and more protective than one named 'Fluffy,' even with identical behavior. This has practical implications: at the vet, at dog parks, and with new people, a name that conveys strength can shape first impressions positively for larger or more powerful breeds.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"details\",\"4\",{\"className\":\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Are there subtle courage names for shy or small pets?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Absolutely. Not every courage name needs to be bold and loud. Consider gentle-but-strong names like Sage (wisdom is courage), Pax (peace requires bravery), Rune (mystery and power), or Fable (stories of heroism). These names convey quiet strength and can perfectly suit a shy cat, a small dog, or a gentle rabbit who shows courage in their own way.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"details\",\"5\",{\"className\":\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\",\"children\":\"What are good courage names for rescue animals?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Rescue pets have already demonstrated real courage by surviving whatever circumstances brought them to you. Names like Phoenix (rising from ashes), Survivor, Chance, Journey, and Valor honor that resilience. Champion, Rocky, and Victor celebrate their fighting spirit. These names tell your pet's story and honor their past while celebrating their present.\"}]]}],\"$L23\"]}]]}]\n1b:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-12\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mb-6\",\"children\":\"🐾 Related Animal Name Generators\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-3 md:grid-cols-4 gap-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"lion\",{\"href\":\"/animal/lion/\",\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-xl p-4 text-center border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:border-primary/30 transition-all group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl mb-1\",\"children\":\"🦁\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold text-gray-700 group-hover:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Lion\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"wolf\",{\"href\":\"/animal/wolf/\",\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-xl p-4 text-center border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:border-primary/30 transition-all group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl mb-1\",\"children\":\"🐺\"